6. Optimize the game: To achieve smooth animation, you can use techniques like double buffering (render to a temporary buffer and swap it with the display buffer), vsync (synchronize with the monitor's refresh rate), and frame rate capping (limit the number of frames per second). You can also use a physics library like Box2D or a game engine like SFML or Godot to simplify the game logic and rendering.

